    {
      "title": "Odisha steps up preparedness as severe cyclonic storm nears Andhra coast",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/odisha-steps-up-preparedness-as-severe-cyclonic-storm-nears-andhra-coast-126102500146_1.html",
      "description": "The Odisha government on Sunday stepped up preparations, mobilising personnel and equipment in vulnerable areas, as a severe cyclonic storm is likely to hit the neighbouring Andhra Pradesh coast on October 28, officials said.\nThe India Meteorological Department (IMD), in its latest bulletin, said a depression over the Bay of Bengal is likely to cross the coast between Bapatla and Visakhapatnam in Andhra Pradesh as a very severe cyclonic storm, with maximum sustained winds of 115-125 kmph and gusts up to 140 kmph.\nThe system is expected to make landfall around the forenoon of October 28, with the predicted landfall area around 300 km from Odisha's Gopalpur, officials said.\nChief Minister Mohan Charan Majhi said that although the system was forecast to make landfall in Andhra Pradesh, the Odisha government would take no chances and remain fully prepared to deal with any eventuality.\nHe directed officials to prioritise public safety, evacuation and emergency response, reiterating the",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-25T07:15:58"
    }
